        ],
        "abstract": "It is argued that we are now approaching the era of electronic data processing where the need for error-free transmission is very important. Here it is necessary that the input to data-processing equipment be free of errors and this will require that those who prepare input data at distant points, as well as the transmission equipments, measure up to the same high standards. Much thought is being given to the selection of alphanumeric codes arranged in such a way that the operator who prepares the card or tape input to the system can recognize a human error. There is an engineering solution for the improvement in accuracy required by the need to transmit data from one point to another. It will merely take a little time for engineers to design the apparatus needed for .each special operation. In most cases the added cost to the customer will be small, but in any event, it will be very much worthwhile in the over-all. Communication people are, as ever, going ahead with progress as required to meet ever-increasing demands for improved accuracy.",
